      "case": "leaves/core/text-range-predicate-family-missing",
      "discriminates": "IsValid ORs its two endpoint tests, so a range with one non-negative endpoint is valid while UndefinedTextRange is not; Contains is half-open, ContainsInclusive admits the end and ContainsExclusive admits neither bound; Intersects treats touching ranges as intersecting where Overlaps does not; and CompareTextRanges falls through to the ends only when the positions tie. The position argument and the comparison result are machine ints rather than the stored int32: a position of 2^32 stays outside the range instead of being folded to 0, WithPos truncates that same argument to 0 the way NewTextRange does, and CompareTextRanges widens both endpoints before subtracting, so the int32 extremes report -4294967295 and 4294967295 where an int32 subtraction would wrap to 1 and -1, which is the wrap Len does report",
